==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|súrr|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|sūraz|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{recons|sūr-|lang=ine-pro}}. Compare English {{term|sour|lang=en}}, German {{term|sauer|lang=de}}, Dutch {{term|zuur|lang=nl}} Danish {{term|sur|lang=da}}, Faroese {{term|súrur|lang=fo}}, Norwegian {{term|sur|lang=no}} and Swedish {{term|sur|lang=sv}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/suːr/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|uːr|lang=is}}

===Adjective===
{{is-adj|súrari|súrastur}}

# [[sour]], [[tart]], [[acid]], [[acidic]]
# (of mood) [[surly]], [[bitter]], [[morose]], [[sour]]
#: ''Ekki vera svona '''súr'''.''
#:: Don't be so '''morose'''.

